  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct and are unchanged: 1 Uno, 1 breadboard, 1 pushbutton, 1 photoresistor, 1 LED, 220 ohm + 2x 10k resistors, 10 jumper wires.",
   "Breadboard mapping: the image's upper half (rows j-f) is bank 'b' and its lower half (rows e-a) is bank 't'. The image's top rails are tp (+) / tn (-) and its bottom rails are bp (+) / bn (-). Rail hole numbers are approximate and do not matter, because each rail is one strip.",
   "The text says analog input 2, but the code, schematic and image use A0, so A0 is used.",
   "LED circuit: pin 9 -> wire3 -> 15b.j, then r1 (220 ohm) 15b.i to 18b.i, then the LED anode (18b.j) and cathode (19b.j), then wire6 from 19b.i to the top ground rail.",
   "Button: side 1 (4b.f / 4t.e) carries pin 2 (wire4) and the 10k pull-down r3 to the ground rail. Side 2 (6b.f / 6t.e) is fed 5V through wire9 from the bottom + rail.",
   "Photoresistor: 14t.c connects to 5V via wire10, and 10t.c connects to A0 (wire5) and to the 10k r2 (to ground), forming the voltage divider.",
   "Power: 5V -> top + rail (wire1) -> bottom + rail (wire7). GND (taken as GND.2) -> top - rail (wire2) -> bottom - rail (wire8)."
  ]
